and they, all together,
the sacred implements to the ground poured down, under man-slaying Lycurgus
being struck with an ox-goad;

and Dionysus, frightened,
went down into the wave of the sea, and Thetis received him in her bosom,
terrified;

There is a city, Ephyre, in the innermost part of horse-pasturing Argos,
and there Sisyphus lived, who became the shrewdest of men,
Sisyphus, Aeolus’-son;

but against him Proetus evils devised in his heart,
who drove him out of the land, since far stronger he was
than the Argives;

But when the evil sign he had received from his son-in-law,
first indeed the Chimaera, the huge one, he bade
kill;

But when he was coming to know him, a god’s good offspring being,
there he held him back, and was giving, he for his part, his own daughter,
and gave him of royal honour half of all;

But when he also was hateful to all the gods,
then he over the plain, the Aleian, alone wandered,
his own heart eating, the path of men avoiding;
